{"id":11,"role":"Tool","content":"path:C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 1511 lines, 93799 bytes --\n   1 | /-\n   2 | # Reflection Positivity on the Lattice\n   3 | \n   4 | Reflection positivity (Osterwalder-Schrader positivity) is the key axiom\n   5 | connecting Euclidean quantum field theory to Minkowski quantum field theory\n   6 | via the OS reconstruction theorem.\n   7 | \n   8 | For SU(N) lattice gauge theory, reflection positivity states:\n   9 | \n  10 |     ⟨f θ(f)⟩ ≥ 0\n  11 | \n  12 | for any observable f depending only on link variables in the positive-time\n  13 | half-lattice (t > 0). Here θ is the time-reflection map:\n  14 | \n  15 |     (θ U)(n, μ) = U(θ n, μ)⁻¹   if μ = 0 (time direction)\n  16 |     (θ U)(n, μ) = U(θ n, μ)     if μ ≠ 0 (spatial direction)\n  17 | -/\n  18 | \n  19 | import YangMills.Lattice\n  20 | import YangMills.SpecialUnitary\n  21 | import YangMills.Proofs.LatticeMeasure\n  22 | import YangMills.Proofs.BasicLemmas\n  23 | \n  24 | set_option linter.unusedVariables false\n  25 | set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000\n  26 | namespace YangMills\n  27 | namespace Lattice\n  28 | \n  29 | /--\n  30 | The reflection of an observable on any lattice type with `ReflectSite`:\n  31 |     (θ f)(U) = f(θ U)\n  32 | where θ acts on link variables via `reflectLinkVariable`.\n  33 | -/\n  34 | def reflectObservable (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [ReflectSite Λ] (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ) :\n  35 |     LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ :=\n  36 |   λ U => f (reflectLinkVariable N U)\n  37 | \n  38 | lemma reflectObservable_involution (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [ReflectSite Λ] (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ)\n  39 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) : reflectObservable N (reflectObservable N f) U = f U := by\n  40 |   dsimp [reflectObservable]\n  41 |   rw [reflection_involution N U]\n  42 | /--\n  43 | The reflection of an observable on ℤ⁴ under the full geometric reflection:\n  44 |     (θ f)(U) = f(θ U)\n  45 | where θ acts on link variables via `reflectLinkVariableZ4`.\n  46 | -/\n  47 | def reflectObservableZ4 (N : ℕ) (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ) : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ :=\n  48 |   λ U => f (reflectLinkVariableZ4 N U)\n  49 | \n  50 | /--\n  51 | The expectation-like pairing for reflection positivity on ℤ⁴.\n  52 | \n  53 | Given a Wilson action S_W and a reference measure dU (product Haar measure),\n  54 | the expectation of an observable F is:\n  55 | \n  56 |     ⟨F⟩ = (1/Z) ∫ F(U) exp(-S_W[U]) dU\n  57 | \n  58 | For the factorization lemma, we only need the formal algebraic structure\n  59 | of this expression. The actual integration theory (Haar measure, product\n  60 | measure, partition function) is available in Mathlib but requires heavy\n  61 | infrastructure. Here we give the symbolic manipulation that underlies\n  62 | the reflection positivity proof.\n  63 | \n  64 | ⚠️ **Known limitation**: The `linearity` field requires integrability hypotheses\n  65 | on `F(extend...)*exp(-β*S)` and `G(extend...)*exp(-β*S)`. This is mathematically\n  66 | correct (linearity of expectation requires integrability). The `reflectionPositive`\n  67 | field relies on `gibbsExpectationZ4_reflection_positive` which has the `hadd` issue\n  68 | documented in `docs/hadd_issue.md`.\n  69 | -/\n  70 | structure Z4Expectation (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (sites : Finset Z4Site) : Type 1 where\n  71 |   /-- The partition function Z = ∫ exp(-S_W) dU. -/\n  72 |   partitionFunction : ℝ\n  73 |   /-- Positivity of the partition function: Z > 0 for β > 0. -/\n  74 |   partitionFunctionPos : partitionFunction > 0\n  75 |   /--\n  76 |   The expectation of an observable F, symbolically:\n  77 |       ⟨F⟩ = (1/Z) ∫ F(U) exp(-S_W[U]) dU\n  78 |   -/\n  79 |   evaluate : (LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ) → ℝ\n  80 |   /--\n  81 |   The expectation is linear: ⟨aF + bG⟩ = a⟨F⟩ + b⟨G⟩,\n  82 |   provided the integrands F(U) exp(-β S_W[U]) and G(U) exp(-β S_W[U]) are integrable\n  83 |   with respect to the product Haar measure.\n  84 |   -/\n  85 |   linearity : ∀ (a b : ℝ) (F G : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ),\n  86 |     (MeasureTheory.Integrable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfigZ4 N sites) => F (extendLinkVariableZ4 N sites cfg) *\n  87 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfigZ4 N β sites cfg)) (productHaarMeasureZ4 N sites)) →\n  88 |     (MeasureTheory.Integrable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfigZ4 N sites) => G (extendLinkVariableZ4 N sites cfg) *\n  89 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfigZ4 N β sites cfg)) (productHaarMeasureZ4 N sites)) →\n  90 |     evaluate (λ U => a * F U + b * G U) = a * evaluate F + b * evaluate G\n  91 |   /--\n  92 |   The expectation is normalized: ⟨1⟩ = 1.\n  93 |   -/\n  94 |   normalization : evaluate (λ _ => 1) = 1\n  95 |   /--\n  96 |   The expectation is positive: if F ≥ 0 pointwise, then ⟨F⟩ ≥ 0.\n  97 |   -/\n  98 |   positivity : ∀ (F : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ),\n  99 |     (∀ U, F U ≥ 0) → evaluate F ≥ 0\n 100 |   /--\n 101 |   Reflection positivity: for any observable f, we have ⟨f θ(f)⟩ ≥ 0.\n 102 |   \n 103 |   This is the conclusion of the Osterwalder-Seiler factorization lemma:\n 104 |   the expectation of f θ(f) is an L² norm squared, hence non-negative.\n 105 |   -/\n 106 |   reflectionPositive : ∀ (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ),\n 107 |     evaluate (λ U => f U * reflectObservableZ4 N f U) ≥ 0\n 108 | \n 109 | /--\n 110 | Construct a `Z4Expectation` for the Wilson action on a finite ℤ⁴ lattice.\n 111 | This provides the reflection positivity certificate for the Wilson action.\n 112 | -/\n 113 | noncomputable def wilsonZ4Expectation (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (sites : Finset Z4Site)\n 114 |     (hadd : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → addVector n 0 ∈ sites)\n 115 |     (hsites : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → reflectSite n ∈ sites) : Z4Expectation N β sites :=\n 116 |   {\n 117 |     partitionFunction := partitionFunctionFiniteZ4 N β sites\n 118 |     partitionFunctionPos := partitionFunctionFiniteZ4_pos N β sites\n 119 |     evaluate := gibbsExpectationZ4 N β sites\n 120 |     linearity := λ a b F G hF hG => gibbsExpectationZ4_linear N β sites a b F G hF hG\n 121 |     normalization := gibbsExpectationZ4_normalization N β sites\n 122 |     positivity := λ F hF => gibbsExpectationZ4_pos N β sites F hF\n 123 |     reflectionPositive := λ f => \n 124 |       gibbsExpectationZ4_reflection_positive N β sites hadd hsites f\n 125 |   }\n 126 | \n 127 | /--\n 128 | The SU(N) lattice Yang-Mills measure with the Wilson action on any finite ℤ⁴ lattice\n 129 | satisfying the closure conditions `hadd` and `hsites` is reflection positive.\n 130 | \n 131 | ⚠️ **Status**: Validated by the Lean kernel. The proof of `gibbsExpectationZ4_reflection_positive`\n 132 | is mathematically vacuous for nonempty finite lattices due to the `hadd` issue (see\n 133 | `docs/hadd_issue.md`). A complete proof requires implementing periodic boundary conditions\n 134 | and the Osterwalder-Seiler factorization.\n 135 | -/\n 136 | theorem lattice_ym_reflection_positive (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (hβ : β > 0)\n 137 |     (sites : Finset Z4Site) (hadd : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → addVector n 0 ∈ sites)\n 138 |     (hsites : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → reflectSite n ∈ sites) :\n 139 |     ∀ (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ),\n 140 |       (wilsonZ4Expectation N β sites hadd hsites).evaluate (λ U => f U * reflectObservableZ4 N f U) ≥ 0 := by\n 141 |   intro f\n 142 |   exact (wilsonZ4Expectation N β sites hadd hsites).reflectionPositive f\n 143 | \n 144 | /-! ### Periodic Lattice (PeriodicSite) -/\n 145 | \n 146 | section PeriodicSite\n 147 | \n 148 | open scoped BigOperators\n 149 | \n 150 | /--\n 151 | Signed lift of `ZMod T` to `ℤ`. For an odd T, this gives a symmetric representation\n 152 | where `t` and `-t` map to opposite integers. The element `0` maps to `0`.\n 153 | -/\n 154 | noncomputable def signedTime (T : ℕ) (t : ZMod T) : ℤ :=\n 155 |   if h : (t.val : ℕ) ≤ (T-1)/2 then (t.val : ℤ) else (t.val : ℤ) - (T : ℤ)\n 156 | \n 157 | lemma signedTime_neg (T : ℕ) [NeZero T] (t : ZMod T) (hT : Odd T) : signedTime T (-t) = -signedTime T t := by\n 158 |   unfold signedTime\n 159 |   have h_val_lt : t.val < T := ZMod.val_lt t\n 160 |   rcases hT with ⟨k, hT⟩\n 161 |   have hTodd : (T : ℤ) = 2*(k : ℤ) + 1 := by exact_mod_cast hT\n 162 |   by_cases hzero : t = 0\n 163 |   · subst hzero; simp\n 164 |   · have hzero_val : t.val ≠ 0 := by rwa [ZMod.val_ne_zero]\n 165 |     haveI : NeZero t := ⟨hzero⟩\n 166 |     have h_neg_val_nat : (-t).val = T - t.val := ZMod.val_neg_of_ne_zero (a := t)\n 167 |     have h_neg_val : ((-t).val : ℤ) = (T : ℤ) - (t.val : ℤ) := by\n 168 |       have h_le : t.val ≤ T := Nat.le_of_lt h_val_lt\n 169 |       simp [h_neg_val_nat, Nat.cast_sub h_le, Nat.cast_ofNat]\n 170 |     split_ifs with h1 h2\n 171 |     · -- Both h1 and h2 hold: ((-t).val : ℕ) ≤ (T-1)/2 and (t.val : ℕ) ≤ (T-1)/2\n 172 |       -- Then (-t).val = T - t.val, and we have T - t.val ≤ (T-1)/2\n 173 |       -- But if t.val ≤ (T-1)/2 then T - t.val > (T-1)/2, contradiction\n 174 |       have : T - t.val > (T-1)/2 := by omega\n 175 |       rw [h_neg_val_nat] at h1\n 176 |       omega\n 177 |     · -- h1 true, h2 false: ((-t).val : ℕ) ≤ (T-1)/2, (t.val : ℕ) > (T-1)/2\n 178 |       rw [h_neg_val_nat] at h1\n 179 |       omega\n 180 |     · -- h1 false, h2 true: ((-t).val : ℕ) > (T-1)/2, (t.val : ℕ) ≤ (T-1)/2\n 181 |       omega\n 182 |     · -- Both false\n 183 |       omega\n 184 | \n 185 | /--\n 186 | The set of lattice sites with positive signed time (strictly positive).\n 187 | -/\n 188 | noncomputable def positiveSites (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] : Finset (PeriodicSite T L) :=\n 189 |   Finset.filter (λ n => signedTime T n.time > 0) Finset.univ\n 190 | \n 191 | /--\n 192 | The set of lattice sites with negative signed time.\n 193 | -/\n 194 | noncomputable def negativeSites (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] : Finset (PeriodicSite T L) :=\n 195 |   Finset.filter (λ n => signedTime T n.time < 0) Finset.univ\n 196 | \n 197 | /--\n 198 | The set of lattice sites at the time interface (signed time = 0).\n 199 | -/\n 200 | noncomputable def interfaceSites (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] : Finset (PeriodicSite T L) :=\n 201 |   Finset.filter (λ n => signedTime T n.time = 0) Finset.univ\n 202 | \n 203 | /--\n 204 | The positive-time part of the Wilson action.\n 205 | -/\n 206 | noncomputable def wilsonActionPeriodicPositive (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n 207 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n 208 |   wilsonActionFinite N β (positiveSites T L) U\n 209 | \n 210 | /--\n 211 | The negative-time part of the Wilson action.\n 212 | -/\n 213 | noncomputable def wilsonActionPeriodicNegative (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n 214 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n 215 |   wilsonActionFinite N β (negativeSites T L) U\n 216 | \n 217 | /--\n 218 | The interface part of the Wilson action.\n 219 | -/\n 220 | noncomputable def wilsonActionPeriodicInterface (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n 221 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n 222 |   wilsonActionFinite N β (interfaceSites T L) U\n 223 | \n 224 | /--\n 225 | The total action decomposes into positive, negative, and interface parts:\n 226 |     S_W = S⁺ + S⁻ + S_int\n 227 | -/\n 228 | lemma total_decomposition_periodic (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n 229 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) :\n 230 |     wilsonActionFinite N β (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) U =\n 231 |     wilsonActionPeriodicPositive N T L β U +\n 232 |     wilsonActionPeriodicNegative N T L β U +\n 233 |     wilsonActionPeriodicInterface N T L β U := by\n 234 |   unfold wilsonActionFinite\n 235 |   have h_cover : (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) =\n 236 |       positiveSites T L ∪ negativeSites T L ∪ interfaceSites T L := by\n 237 |     ext n; simp [positiveSites, negativeSites, interfaceSites]\n 238 |     by_cases hpos : signedTime T n.time > 0\n 239 |     · simp [hpos]\n 240 |     · by_cases hneg : signedTime T n.time < 0\n 241 |       · simp [hpos, hneg]\n 242 |       · have hzero : signedTime T n.time = 0 := by\n 243 |           have hle : signedTime T n.time ≤ 0 := by linarith\n 244 |           have hge : signedTime T n.time ≥ 0 := by linarith\n 245 |           linarith\n 246 |         simp [hpos, hneg, hzero]\n 247 |   rw [h_cover]\n 248 |   have h_disjoint_pos_neg : Disjoint (positiveSites T L) (negativeSites T L) := by\n 249 |     unfold positiveSites negativeSites\n 250 |     rw [Finset.disjoint_filter]\n 251 |     intro n hn hpos\n 252 |     intro hneg\n 253 |     linarith\n 254 |   have h_disjoint_neg_int : Disjoint (negativeSites T L) (interfaceSites T L) := by\n 255 |     unfold negativeSites interfaceSites\n 256 |     rw [Finset.disjoint_filter]\n 257 |     intro n hn hneg\n 258 |     intro hzero\n 259 |     linarith\n 260 |   have h_disjoint_pos_int : Disjoint (positiveSites T L) (interfaceSites T L) := by\n 261 |     unfold positiveSites interfaceSites\n 262 |     rw [Finset.disjoint_filter]\n 263 |     intro n hn hpos\n 264 |     intro hzero\n 265 |     linarith\n 266 |   have h_disjoint_union_int : Disjoint (positiveSites T L ∪ negativeSites T L) (interfaceSites T L) := by\n 267 |     rw [Finset.disjoint_union_left]\n 268 |     exact ⟨h_disjoint_pos_int, h_disjoint_neg_int⟩\n 269 |   calc\n 270 |     ∑ n ∈ (positiveSites T L ∪ negativeSites T L) ∪ interfaceSites T L,\n 271 |         ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4, plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n 272 |         = (∑ n ∈ positiveSites T L ∪ negativeSites T L,\n 273 |             ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4, plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν) +\n 274 |           (∑ n ∈ interfaceSites T L,\n 275 |             ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4, plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν) := by\n 276 |       rw [Finset.sum_union h_disjoint_union_int]\n 277 |     _ = (∑ n ∈ positiveSites T L,\n 278 |             ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4, plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν) +\n 279 |         (∑ n ∈ negativeSites T L,\n 280 |             ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4, plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν) +\n 281 |         (∑ n ∈ interfaceSites T L,\n 282 |             ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4, plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν) := by\n 283 |       rw [Finset.sum_union h_disjoint_pos_neg, add_assoc]\n 284 |     _ = wilsonActionPeriodicPositive N T L β U + wilsonActionPeriodicNegative N T L β U +\n 285 |         wilsonActionPeriodicInterface N T L β U := by\n 286 |       unfold wilsonActionPeriodicPositive wilsonActionPeriodicNegative wilsonActionPeriodicInterface wilsonActionFinite\n 287 |       rfl\n 288 | /-! ### Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition (plaquette-based) -/\n 289 | \n 290 | section OSDecomposition\n 291 | \n 292 | open Matrix\n 293 | open scoped BigOperators\n 294 | \n 295 | /-- Index type for oriented plaquettes on a periodic lattice: (base site, μ, ν). -/\n 296 | abbrev PlaquetteIndex (T L : ℕ) : Type := PeriodicSite T L × Fin 4 × Fin 4\n 297 | \n 298 | instance (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] : Fintype (PlaquetteIndex T L) :=\n 299 |   inferInstanceAs (Fintype (PeriodicSite T L × Fin 4 × Fin 4))\n 300 | \n 301 | /-- Cyclic permutation of trace for 4 matrices: Tr(ABCD) = Tr(BCDA). -/\n 302 | lemma trace_cyclic_four (N : ℕ) (A B C D : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ) :\n 303 |     Matrix.trace (A * B * C * D) = Matrix.trace (B * C * D * A) := by\n 304 |   calc\n 305 |     Matrix.trace (A * B * C * D) = Matrix.trace (D * (A * B * C)) := by\n 306 |       rw [trace_mul_comm (A * B * C) D]\n 307 |     _ = Matrix.trace (D * A * B * C) := by noncomm_ring\n 308 |     _ = Matrix.trace ((D * A) * (B * C)) := by noncomm_ring\n 309 |     _ = Matrix.trace ((B * C) * (D * A)) := trace_mul_comm (D * A) (B * C)\n 310 |     _ = Matrix.trace (B * C * D * A) := by noncomm_ring\n 311 | \n 312 | /-- For A ∈ SU(N), Re Tr(A) = Re Tr(A⁻¹). -/\n 313 | lemma trace_re_inv (N : ℕ) (A : SU N) :\n 314 |     ((Matrix.trace ((A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ) =\n 315 |     ((Matrix.trace (((A⁻¹ : SU N) : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ) := by\n 316 |   have hstar : (A⁻¹ : SU N) = (star A : SU N) := by\n 317 |     simpa using (Matrix.star_eq_inv (A : SU N)).symm\n 318 |   have h_trace_star : Matrix.trace (star ((A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))) =\n 319 |       star (Matrix.trace ((A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))) := by\n 320 |     simp [Matrix.trace, map_sum]\n 321 |   calc\n 322 |     ((Matrix.trace ((A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ) =\n 323 |         ((star (Matrix.trace ((A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ)))).re : ℝ) := by simp\n 324 |     _ = ((Matrix.trace (star ((A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ)))).re : ℝ) := by\n 325 |       simp [h_trace_star]\n 326 |     _ = ((Matrix.trace (((A⁻¹ : SU N) : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ) := by simp [hstar]\n 327 | \n 328 | /-- The sum over all oriented plaquettes (n; μ, ν) where all four corners have\n 329 | positive signed time. This is the correct positive-time part of the\n 330 | Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition. -/\n 331 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSPositive (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n 332 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n 333 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n 334 |     if signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n 335 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n 336 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0 then\n 337 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n 338 |     else 0\n 339 | \n 340 | /-- The sum over all oriented plaquettes (n; μ, ν) where all four corners have\n 341 | negative signed time. This is the correct negative-time part of the\n 342 | Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition. -/\n 343 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSNegative (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n 344 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n 345 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n 346 |     if signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n 347 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n 348 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0 then\n 349 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n 350 |     else 0\n 351 | \n 352 | /-- The sum over the remaining oriented plaquettes (those with corners on both sides\n 353 | of the time interface). This is the interface part of the\n 354 | Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition. -/\n 355 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSInterface (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n 356 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n 357 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n 358 |     if ¬ (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n 359 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n 360 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∧\n 361 |        ¬ (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n 362 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n 363 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0) then\n 364 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n 365 |     else 0\n 366 | \n 367 | /--\n 368 | For each oriented plaquette (n; μ, ν), exactly one of the three conditions holds:\n 369 | positive (all corners > 0), negative (all corners < 0), or interface (the rest).\n 370 | -/\n 371 | lemma plaquette_classification (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (n : PeriodicSite T L) (μ ν : Fin 4) :\n 372 |     (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n 373 |      signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n 374 |      signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∨\n 375 |     (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n 376 |      signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n 377 |      signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0) ∨\n 378 |     (¬ (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n 379 |         signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n 380 |         signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∧\n 381 |      ¬ (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n 382 |         signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n 383 |         signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0)) := by\n 384 |   by_cases hpos : signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n 385 |                   signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n 386 |                   signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0\n 387 |   · exact Or.inl hpos\n 388 |   · by_cases hneg : signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n 389 |                    signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n 390 |                    signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0\n 391 |     · exact Or.inr (Or.inl hneg)\n 392 |     · exact Or.inr (Or.inr ⟨hpos, hneg⟩)\n 393 | \n 394 | /--\n 395 | The total Wilson action decomposes into positive, negative, and interface parts\n 396 | (plaquette-based OS decomposition):\n 397 |     S_W = S_OS⁺ + S_OS⁻ + S_OS_int\n 398 | -/\n 399 | lemma total_decomposition_os_periodic (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n 400 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) :\n 401 |     wilsonActionFinite N β (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) U =\n 402 |     wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β U +\n 403 |     wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β U +\n 404 |     wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U := by\n 405 |   unfold wilsonActionOSPositive wilsonActi