{"id":15,"role":"Tool","content":"path:C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Lattice.lean\n-- 351 lines, 12085 bytes --\n  1 | /-\n  2 | # Lattice Gauge Theory\n  3 | \n  4 | Formalization of lattice gauge theory: Wilson action, plaquette variables,\n  5 | and the continuum limit.\n  6 | \n  7 | References:\n  8 | - K. Wilson, \"Confinement of quarks\" (1974)\n  9 | - T. Balaban, \"Renormalization group approach to lattice gauge field theories\"\n 10 | - J. Glimm, A. Jaffe, \"Quantum Physics: A Functional Integral Point of View\"\n 11 | -/\n 12 | \n 13 | import YangMills.SpecialUnitary\n 14 | import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace\n 15 | \n 16 | open Matrix\n 17 | open scoped Matrix\n 18 | open scoped BigOperators\n 19 | \n 20 | namespace YangMills\n 21 | \n 22 | namespace Lattice\n 23 | \n 24 | /-! ### Typeclasses for lattice operations -/\n 25 | \n 26 | /--\n 27 | Typeclass for adding a basis vector to a lattice site in direction μ.\n 28 | -/\n 29 | class AddVector (Λ : Type) where\n 30 |   addVector : Λ → Fin 4 → Λ\n 31 | \n 32 | /--\n 33 | Typeclass for reflecting a lattice site in the time direction.\n 34 | The `involution` field ensures that reflecting twice is the identity.\n 35 | -/\n 36 | class ReflectSite (Λ : Type) where\n 37 |   reflectSite : Λ → Λ\n 38 |   involution : ∀ n, reflectSite (reflectSite n) = n\n 39 | \n 40 | /-! ### The ℤ⁴ lattice -/\n 41 | \n 42 | /--\n 43 | A site in the ℤ⁴ lattice, represented as a 4-tuple of integers.\n 44 | This is the default index set for a hypercubic lattice.\n 45 | -/\n 46 | abbrev Z4Site : Type := ℤ × ℤ × ℤ × ℤ\n 47 | \n 48 | /--\n 49 | Add the μ-th standard basis vector to a Z4Site.\n 50 | Given n = (n₀, n₁, n₂, n₃) and μ ∈ {0,1,2,3}, returns n + e_μ.\n 51 | -/\n 52 | def addVectorZ4 (n : Z4Site) (μ : Fin 4) : Z4Site :=\n 53 |   match μ with\n 54 |   | 0 => (n.1 + 1, n.2.1, n.2.2.1, n.2.2.2)\n 55 |   | 1 => (n.1, n.2.1 + 1, n.2.2.1, n.2.2.2)\n 56 |   | 2 => (n.1, n.2.1, n.2.2.1 + 1, n.2.2.2)\n 57 |   | 3 => (n.1, n.2.1, n.2.2.1, n.2.2.2 + 1)\n 58 | \n 59 | /--\n 60 | Convenience alias for `addVectorZ4` for backward compatibility.\n 61 | -/\n 62 | def addVector (n : Z4Site) (μ : Fin 4) : Z4Site := addVectorZ4 n μ\n 63 | \n 64 | instance : AddVector Z4Site where\n 65 |   addVector := addVectorZ4\n 66 | \n 67 | /--\n 68 | The time direction index. In ℝ⁴ with coordinates (x₀, x₁, x₂, x₃),\n 69 | the 0-th coordinate is Euclidean time.\n 70 | -/\n 71 | def timeDirection : Fin 4 := 0\n 72 | \n 73 | /--\n 74 | The time-reflection map θ acting on lattice sites for the ℤ⁴ lattice.\n 75 | On a lattice with spacing a, the site n = (n₀, n₁, n₂, n₃) ∈ ℤ⁴ is\n 76 | reflected to n' = (-n₀, n₁, n₂, n₃).\n 77 | -/\n 78 | def reflectSiteZ4 (n : Z4Site) : Z4Site :=\n 79 |   (-n.1, n.2.1, n.2.2.1, n.2.2.2)\n 80 | \n 81 | /--\n 82 | Convenience alias for `reflectSiteZ4` for backward compatibility.\n 83 | -/\n 84 | def reflectSite (n : Z4Site) : Z4Site := reflectSiteZ4 n\n 85 | \n 86 | instance : ReflectSite Z4Site where\n 87 |   reflectSite := reflectSiteZ4\n 88 |   involution n := by\n 89 |     dsimp [reflectSiteZ4]; simp\n 90 | \n 91 | /--\n 92 | reflectSite is involutive: θ(θ n) = n.\n 93 | -/\n 94 | lemma reflectSite_involution (n : Z4Site) : reflectSite (reflectSite n) = n :=\n 95 |   ReflectSite.involution n\n 96 | \n 97 | /-! ### The periodic lattice -/\n 98 | \n 99 | /--\n100 | A site in a periodic lattice with `T` time slices and `L³` spatial sites.\n101 | The time coordinate lives in `ZMod T` (cyclic group of order T), and each\n102 | spatial coordinate lives in `ZMod L`. This gives periodic boundary conditions\n103 | in all directions.\n104 | -/\n105 | @[ext] structure PeriodicSite (T L : ℕ) : Type where\n106 |   /-- Time coordinate modulo T (cycles around). -/\n107 |   time : ZMod T\n108 |   /-- Spatial x coordinate modulo L. -/\n109 |   x : ZMod L\n110 |   /-- Spatial y coordinate modulo L. -/\n111 |   y : ZMod L\n112 |   /-- Spatial z coordinate modulo L. -/\n113 |   z : ZMod L\n114 |   deriving DecidableEq\n115 | instance (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] : Fintype (PeriodicSite T L) :=\n116 |   Fintype.ofEquiv (ZMod T × ZMod L × ZMod L × ZMod L) {\n117 |     toFun := λ ((t, x, y, z) : ZMod T × ZMod L × ZMod L × ZMod L) => \n118 |       { time := t, x := x, y := y, z := z }\n119 |     invFun := λ n => (n.time, n.x, n.y, n.z)\n120 |     left_inv := λ _ => rfl\n121 |     right_inv := λ _ => rfl\n122 |   }\n123 | \n124 | /--\n125 | Add the μ-th standard basis vector to a `PeriodicSite`.\n126 | All coordinates use `ZMod` addition, which wraps around automatically.\n127 | -/\n128 | def addVectorPeriodic (T L : ℕ) (n : PeriodicSite T L) (μ : Fin 4) : PeriodicSite T L :=\n129 |   match μ with\n130 |   | 0 => { n with time := n.time + 1 }\n131 |   | 1 => { n with x := n.x + 1 }\n132 |   | 2 => { n with y := n.y + 1 }\n133 |   | 3 => { n with z := n.z + 1 }\n134 | \n135 | instance (T L : ℕ) : AddVector (PeriodicSite T L) where\n136 |   addVector := addVectorPeriodic T L\n137 | \n138 | /--\n139 | Time reflection on a periodic lattice: maps time t ↦ -t (mod T).\n140 | This is involutive because -(-t) = t in ZMod T.\n141 | -/\n142 | def reflectSitePeriodic (T L : ℕ) (n : PeriodicSite T L) : PeriodicSite T L :=\n143 |   { n with time := -n.time }\n144 | \n145 | instance (T L : ℕ) : ReflectSite (PeriodicSite T L) where\n146 |   reflectSite := reflectSitePeriodic T L\n147 |   involution n := by\n148 |     dsimp [reflectSitePeriodic]; simp\n149 | \n150 | /--\n151 | `reflectSitePeriodic` is involutive: θ(θ n) = n.\n152 | -/\n153 | lemma reflectSitePeriodic_involution (T L : ℕ) (n : PeriodicSite T L) :\n154 |     reflectSitePeriodic T L (reflectSitePeriodic T L n) = n :=\n155 |   ReflectSite.involution n\n156 | \n157 | \n158 | /-- A finite lattice Λ ⊂ ℤ⁴ as a hypercube with spacing a > 0. -/\n159 | structure Lattice (Λ : Type) : Type 1 where\n160 |   /-- Lattice spacing (a real number > 0). -/\n161 |   spacing : ℝ\n162 |   /-- The set of lattice sites. -/\n163 |   sites : Λ\n164 |   /-- Adjacency relation for links. -/\n165 |   links : Λ → Λ → Prop\n166 |   /-- Plaquettes are ordered 4-tuples of sites forming a square. -/\n167 |   plaquettes : (Λ × Λ × Λ × Λ) → Prop\n168 | \n169 | /-- A gauge field configuration on the lattice: each directed link (x → x + a e_μ)\n170 | carries a group element U(x, μ) ∈ G. -/\n171 | @[ext]\n172 | structure LinkVariable (G : Type) (Λ : Type) : Type 1 where\n173 |   /-- Assigns a group element to each lattice site and direction. -/\n174 |   value : Λ → Fin 4 → G\n175 | \n176 | /--\n177 | The reflection map θ on link variables for any lattice type with `ReflectSite`.\n178 | For a link variable U(n, μ) from site n in direction μ, the reflected\n179 | link variable is:\n180 | \n181 |     (θ U)(n, μ) = U(θ n, μ)⁻¹   if μ = 0 (time direction)\n182 |     (θ U)(n, μ) = U(θ n, μ)     if μ ≠ 0 (spatial direction)\n183 | \n184 | The inverse appears for time-like links because reflection reverses the\n185 | orientation of the link in time.\n186 | -/\n187 | def reflectLinkVariable (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [ReflectSite Λ] (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) :\n188 |     LinkVariable (SU N) Λ :=\n189 |   {\n190 |     value := λ n μ =>\n191 |       if μ = 0 then\n192 |         (U.value (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) μ)⁻¹\n193 |       else\n194 |         U.value (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) μ\n195 |   }\n196 | \n197 | /--\n198 | The full geometric reflection is involutive: θ(θ U) = U.\n199 | -/\n200 | lemma reflection_involution (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [ReflectSite Λ] (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) :\n201 |     reflectLinkVariable N (reflectLinkVariable N U) = U := by\n202 |   ext n μ\n203 |   dsimp [reflectLinkVariable]\n204 |   have h_inv : ReflectSite.reflectSite (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) = n := ReflectSite.involution n\n205 |   by_cases h : μ = 0\n206 |   · subst h; simp [h_inv]\n207 |   · simp [h, h_inv]\n208 | \n209 | /--\n210 | Convenience alias for `reflectLinkVariable` on `Z4Site` for backward compatibility.\n211 | -/\n212 | def reflectLinkVariableZ4 (N : ℕ) (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site) : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site :=\n213 |   reflectLinkVariable N U\n214 | \n215 | /--\n216 | The full geometric reflection is involutive on Z4Site: θ(θ U) = U.\n217 | -/\n218 | lemma reflection_involution_z4 (N : ℕ) (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site) :\n219 |     reflectLinkVariableZ4 N (reflectLinkVariableZ4 N U) = U :=\n220 |   reflection_involution N U\n221 | \n222 | section PlaquetteProduct\n223 | \n224 | /--\n225 | The ordered product of link variables around an elementary plaquette in a\n226 | lattice with `AddVector`. For a site n and directions μ, ν, the product traverses:\n227 | \n228 |     n + e_μ + e_ν ←── n + e_ν\n229 |          |              ↑\n230 |          |              |\n231 |          ↓              |\n232 |     n + e_μ  ────────── n\n233 | \n234 | Explicitly: U(n, μ) · U(n+e_μ, ν) · U(n+e_μ+e_ν, μ)⁻¹ · U(n+e_ν, ν)⁻¹\n235 | \n236 | The inverse for the third and fourth links accounts for the orientation\n237 | reversal (traversing the link backwards).\n238 | -/\n239 | noncomputable def plaquetteProduct (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [AddVector Λ]\n240 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) (n : Λ) (μ ν : Fin 4) : SU N :=\n241 |   U.value n μ *\n242 |   U.value (AddVector.addVector n μ) ν *\n243 |   (U.value (AddVector.addVector (AddVector.addVector n μ) ν) μ)⁻¹ *\n244 |   (U.value (AddVector.addVector n ν) ν)⁻¹\n245 | \n246 | /--\n247 | The contribution of a single oriented plaquette to the Wilson action:\n248 | \n249 |     S_p = β (1 - (1/N) Re Tr(U_∂p))\n250 | \n251 | where U_∂p is the plaquette product. For SU(N) matrices, Tr(U) ∈ ℂ and\n252 | Re Tr(U) ∈ ℝ. The term (1 - (1/N) Re Tr) is non-negative and vanishes when\n253 | U_∂p = 1.\n254 | -/\n255 | noncomputable def plaquetteContribution (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) {Λ : Type} [AddVector Λ]\n256 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) (n : Λ) (μ ν : Fin 4) : ℝ :=\n257 |   β * ((1 : ℝ) - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N U n μ ν : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re))\n258 | \n259 | /--\n260 | The total Wilson action for a finite set of lattice sites.\n261 | For each site n ∈ sites, sum over all oriented plaquettes (n; μ, ν).\n262 | \n263 | Explicitly:\n264 |     S_W[U] = ∑_{n} ∑_{μ,ν} β (1 - (1/N) Re Tr(U_∂p(n,μ,ν)))\n265 | \n266 | In the standard Wilson action, the sum is over unordered plaquette orientations\n267 | (μ < ν). The sum over all ordered pairs (μ,ν) double-counts each unoriented\n268 | plaquette; the coupling constant β can absorb this factor.\n269 | -/\n270 | noncomputable def wilsonActionFinite (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) {Λ : Type} [AddVector Λ]\n271 |     (sites : Finset Λ) (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) : ℝ :=\n272 |   ∑ n ∈ sites, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4, plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n273 | \n274 | /--\n275 | The partition function for a finite lattice with the Wilson action.\n276 | For a finite lattice with site set `sites` and coupling β > 0:\n277 | \n278 |     Z(β) = ∫ exp(-S_W[U]) dμ₀(U)\n279 | \n280 | where μ₀ is the product Haar measure on SU(N)^(sites × Fin 4).\n281 | \n282 | Note: The actual definition (as `partitionFunctionFinite`) is in\n283 | `LatticeMeasure.lean` as it requires the Haar measure on SU(N).\n284 | As a placeholder we define a stub that just returns 1.\n285 | -/\n286 | noncomputable def partitionFunctionFiniteStub (_N : ℕ) (_β : ℝ) {Λ : Type} (_sites : Finset Λ) : ℝ := 1\n287 | \n288 | end PlaquetteProduct\n289 | \n290 | /--\n291 | The Wilson plaquette action (abstract interface):\n292 |   S_W[U] = β ∑_p (1 - (1/N) Re Tr U_∂p)\n293 | where the sum is over all plaquettes p, and U_∂p is the ordered product of\n294 | link variables around the plaquette.\n295 | -/\n296 | structure WilsonAction (G : Type) (Λ : Type) : Type 1 where\n297 |   /-- The coupling constant β = 2N/g² (placeholder ℝ). -/\n298 |   beta : ℝ\n299 |   /-- Evaluate the action on a link configuration. -/\n300 |   evaluate : LinkVariable G Λ → ℝ\n301 | \n302 | /--\n303 | The lattice Yang-Mills measure (Gibbs measure):\n304 |   dμ(U) = (1/Z) exp(-S_W[U]) ∏_{links} dU_link\n305 | where dU_link is the Haar measure on G.\n306 | -/\n307 | structure LatticeMeasure (G : Type) (Λ : Type) : Type 1 where\n308 |   /-- Partition function Z = ∫ exp(-S_W) ∏ dU. -/\n309 |   partitionFunction : ℝ\n310 |   /-- Density with respect to product Haar measure. -/\n311 |   density : LinkVariable G Λ → ℝ\n312 | \n313 | /--\n314 | Continuum limit: as lattice spacing a → 0, the lattice theory should converge\n315 | to the continuum Yang-Mills theory.\n316 | \n317 | More precisely, let μ_a be the lattice Yang-Mills measure on a lattice with\n318 | spacing a > 0. We require:\n319 | \n320 | 1. **Convergence of Schwinger functions**: For each n, the lattice Schwinger\n321 |    functions S_n^{(a)} converge to continuum Schwinger functions S_n as a → 0,\n322 |    in the sense of tempered distributions.\n323 | \n324 | 2. **OS axioms for the limit**: The limiting Schwinger functions {S_n} satisfy\n325 |    the Osterwalder-Schrader axioms (OS0-OS4), so the OS reconstruction theorem\n326 |    yields a Wightman QFT.\n327 | \n328 | 3. **Mass gap**: The limiting theory has a positive mass gap: the Hamiltonian\n329 |    has a spectral gap above the vacuum, and truncated correlation functions\n330 |    decay exponentially.\n331 | \n332 | This is the hardest part of the Yang-Mills problem and is the subject of\n333 | Balaban's renormalization group approach. In the lattice gauge theory\n334 | literature, this is often called \"taking the continuum limit.\"\n335 | \n336 | References:\n337 | - T. Balaban, \"Renormalization group approach to lattice gauge field theories\"\n338 | - J. Glimm, A. Jaffe, \"Quantum Physics: A Functional Integral Point of View\"\n339 | - M. Salmhofer, \"Renormalization: An Introduction\"\n340 | -/\n341 | structure ContinuumLimit (N : ℕ) : Prop where\n342 |   /-- For each n, the lattice Schwinger functions converge as a → 0. -/\n343 |   schwingerFunctionsConverge : True\n344 |   /-- The limiting Schwinger functions satisfy the OS axioms. -/\n345 |   limitingFunctionsSatisfyOS : True\n346 |   /-- The limiting Wightman QFT has a positive mass gap. -/\n347 |   massGapPositivity : True\n348 | \n349 | end Lattice\n350 | \n351 | end YangMills\n\n---\npath:C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\LatticeMeasure.lean\n-- 521 lines, 30684 bytes --\n  1 | /-\n  2 | # Lattice Yang-Mills Measure\n  3 | -/\n  4 | import YangMills.Lattice\n  5 | import YangMills.SpecialUnitary\n  6 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Haar.Basic\n  7 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Pi\n  8 | import Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Constructions.Pi\n  9 | \n 10 | open Set Matrix MeasureTheory\n 11 | open scoped MeasureTheory\n 12 | open Complex\n 13 | \n 14 | namespace YangMills\n 15 | namespace Lattice\n 16 | \n 17 | /-- MeasurableSpace on `LinkVariable` induced by the `value` projection. -/\n 18 | instance {G : Type} {Λ : Type} [MeasurableSpace G] :\n 19 |     MeasurableSpace (LinkVariable G Λ) :=\n 20 |   MeasurableSpace.comap (fun U => U.value) inferInstance\n 21 | \n 22 | section LinkSet\n 23 | def LinkSet (Λ : Type) : Type := Λ × Fin 4\n 24 | abbrev LinkConfig (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) : Type := LinkSet Λ → SU N\n 25 | def linkVariableToConfig (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) : LinkConfig N Λ :=\n 26 |   λ (site, μ) => U.value site μ\n 27 | def configToLinkVariable (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) (U : LinkConfig N Λ) : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ :=\n 28 |   { value := λ site μ => U (site, μ) }\n 29 | lemma linkVariableConfig_bijection (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) :\n 30 |     configToLinkVariable N Λ (linkVariableToConfig N Λ U) = U := by\n 31 |   ext site μ; simp [linkVariableToConfig, configToLinkVariable]\n 32 | lemma configLinkVariable_bijection (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) (U : LinkConfig N Λ) :\n 33 |     linkVariableToConfig N Λ (configToLinkVariable N Λ U) = U := by\n 34 |   ext ⟨site, μ⟩; simp [linkVariableToConfig, configToLinkVariable]\n 35 | end LinkSet\n 36 | \n 37 | section ProductHaarMeasure\n 38 | \n 39 | section GenericProductMeasure\n 40 | \n 41 | /-- The index set of links in a finite lattice: pairs (site, direction) where site ∈ sites. -/\n 42 | def FiniteLinkIndex (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ) : Type :=\n 43 |   Subtype (λ (x : Λ × Fin 4) => x.1 ∈ sites)\n 44 | \n 45 | instance (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ) : Fintype (FiniteLinkIndex Λ sites) :=\n 46 |   Fintype.subtype (sites.product (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin 4))) (by intro x; simp)\n 47 | \n 48 | /-- A link configuration on a finite lattice is an assignment of SU(N) group elements\n 49 | to each directed link (site, μ) where site ∈ sites. -/\n 50 | abbrev FiniteLinkConfig (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ) : Type :=\n 51 |   FiniteLinkIndex Λ sites → SU N\n 52 | \n 53 | /-- Product Haar measure on SU(N)^{sites × {0,1,2,3}}. -/\n 54 | noncomputable def productHaarMeasure (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ) :\n 55 |     Measure (FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) :=\n 56 |   let K : TopologicalSpace.PositiveCompacts (SU N) :=\n 57 |     ⟨⟨Set.univ, isCompact_univ⟩, by simpa using Set.univ_nonempty (α := SU N)⟩\n 58 |   MeasureTheory.Measure.pi (λ _ : FiniteLinkIndex Λ sites => MeasureTheory.Measure.haarMeasure K)\n 59 | \n 60 | /-- Extend a configuration on `sites` to a full link variable by setting missing links to 1. -/\n 61 | noncomputable def extendLinkVariable (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ)\n 62 |     (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ :=\n 63 |   { value := λ n μ => if h : n ∈ sites then U ⟨(n, μ), h⟩ else 1 }\n 64 | \n 65 | /-- Restrict a full link variable to a configuration on `sites`. -/\n 66 | noncomputable def restrictLinkVariable (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ)\n 67 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites :=\n 68 |   λ ⟨(n, μ), hn⟩ => U.value n μ\n 69 | \n 70 | /-- The Wilson action evaluated on a finite-link configuration. -/\n 71 | noncomputable def wilsonActionFiniteConfig (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] [AddVector Λ]\n 72 |     (sites : Finset Λ) (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) : ℝ :=\n 73 |   wilsonActionFinite N β sites (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg)\n 74 | \n 75 | /-- `extendLinkVariable` is measurable: each component is either an evaluation (measurable)\n 76 | or a constant (measurable), depending on whether the site is in the lattice. -/\n 77 | lemma measurable_extendLinkVariable (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ) :\n 78 |     Measurable (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites) := by\n 79 |   have h : Measurable ((fun U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ => U.value) ∘ extendLinkVariable N Λ sites) := by\n 80 |     show Measurable (fun (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) (n : Λ) (μ : Fin 4) =>\n 81 |       if h : n ∈ sites then U ⟨(n, μ), h⟩ else (1 : SU N))\n 82 |     rw [measurable_pi_iff]\n 83 |     intro n\n 84 |     rw [measurable_pi_iff]\n 85 |     intro μ\n 86 |     by_cases h : n ∈ sites\n 87 |     · simp only [h, if_pos]\n 88 |       exact measurable_pi_apply (⟨(n, μ), h⟩ : FiniteLinkIndex Λ sites)\n 89 |     · simp only [h, if_neg]\n 90 |       exact measurable_const\n 91 |   exact measurable_comap_iff.mpr h\n 92 | \n 93 | /-- `LinkVariable.value` is surjective: every function comes from a LinkVariable. -/\n 94 | lemma LinkVariable.value_surjective (G : Type) (Λ : Type) :\n 95 |     Function.Surjective (fun (U : LinkVariable G Λ) => U.value) := by\n 96 |   intro f; exact ⟨{ value := f }, rfl⟩\n 97 | \n 98 | /-- `wilsonActionFiniteConfig` is measurable, expressed as a finite sum of measurable terms.\n 99 | Each term `plaquetteContribution N β (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg) n μ ν` is measurable\n100 | because it depends on `cfg` at finitely many indices via continuous SU(N) operations\n101 | (multiplication, inversion, trace, real part). -/\n102 | lemma measurable_wilsonActionFiniteConfig (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] [AddVector Λ]\n103 |     (sites : Finset Λ) : Measurable (wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites) := by\n104 |   unfold wilsonActionFiniteConfig wilsonActionFinite\n105 |   refine Finset.measurable_sum _ (λ n hn => ?_)\n106 |   refine Finset.measurable_sum _ (λ μ hμ => ?_)\n107 |   refine Finset.measurable_sum _ (λ ν hν => ?_)\n108 |   unfold plaquetteContribution\n109 |   -- Each term: β * (1 - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace (plaquetteProduct ...)).re : ℝ))\n110 |   -- Show the innermost part (trace ...).re is measurable\n111 |   have h_meas_inner : Measurable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) =>\n112 |     ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg) n μ ν : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ)) := by\n113 |     have h_cont_trace_re : Continuous (λ (g : SU N) => ((trace ((g : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ)) := by\n114 |       -- trace = λ A => ∑ᵢ Aᵢᵢ is continuous as a sum of projections\n115 |       have h_cont_trace : Continuous (trace : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ → ℂ) := by\n116 |         have h_eq : trace = λ (A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ) => ∑ i : Fin N, A i i := by\n117 |           ext A; simp [Matrix.trace]\n118 |         rw [h_eq]\n119 |         refine continuous_finsetSum Finset.univ (λ i hi => ?_)\n120 |         -- A i i is the (i,i) entry, which is continuous\n121 |         have h_entry : Continuous (λ (A : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ) => A i i) :=\n122 |           (continuous_apply i).comp (continuous_apply i)\n123 |         exact h_entry\n124 |       -- The inclusion SU N → Matrix is continuous (subtype)\n125 |       have h_cont_val : Continuous (Subtype.val : SU N → Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ) :=\n126 |         continuous_subtype_val\n127 |       -- re is continuous\n128 |       have h_cont_re : Continuous (Complex.re : ℂ → ℝ) := Complex.continuous_re\n129 |       -- Composition: g ↦ (g : Matrix) ↦ trace(...) ↦ re(trace)\n130 |       exact h_cont_re.comp (h_cont_trace.comp h_cont_val)\n131 |     have h_cont_pp : Continuous (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) =>\n132 |       plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg) n μ ν) := by\n133 |       have h_val_cont (n' : Λ) (μ' : Fin 4) : Continuous (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) =>\n134 |         (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg).value n' μ') := by\n135 |         by_cases h : n' ∈ sites\n136 |         · have h_eq : (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) => (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg).value n' μ') =\n137 |             (λ cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites => cfg ⟨(n', μ'), h⟩) := by\n138 |             ext cfg; simp [extendLinkVariable, h]\n139 |           rw [h_eq]\n140 |           exact continuous_apply (⟨(n', μ'), h⟩ : FiniteLinkIndex Λ sites)\n141 |         · have h_eq : (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) => (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg).value n' μ') =\n142 |             (λ _ : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites => (1 : SU N)) := by\n143 |             ext cfg; simp [extendLinkVariable, h]\n144 |           rw [h_eq]\n145 |           exact continuous_const\n146 |       unfold plaquetteProduct\n147 |       have h_ab : Continuous (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) =>\n148 |         (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg).value n μ * (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg).value (AddVector.addVector n μ) ν) :=\n149 |         Continuous.mul (h_val_cont n μ) (h_val_cont (AddVector.addVector n μ) ν)\n150 |       have h_abc : Continuous (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) =>\n151 |         (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg).value n μ * (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg).value (AddVector.addVector n μ) ν *\n152 |         ((extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg).value (AddVector.addVector (AddVector.addVector n μ) ν) μ)⁻¹) :=\n153 |         Continuous.mul h_ab (Continuous.inv (h_val_cont (AddVector.addVector (AddVector.addVector n μ) ν) μ))\n154 |       exact Continuous.mul h_abc (Continuous.inv (h_val_cont (AddVector.addVector n ν) ν))\n155 |     have h_cont_total : Continuous (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) =>\n156 |       ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg) n μ ν : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ)) :=\n157 |       h_cont_trace_re.comp h_cont_pp\n158 |     haveI : OpensMeasurableSpace (FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) := by\n159 |       infer_instance\n160 |     exact h_cont_total.measurable\n161 |   have h_term : Measurable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) =>\n162 |     β * ((1 : ℝ) - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites cfg) n μ ν :\n163 |       Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ))) := by\n164 |     refine Measurable.const_mul (Measurable.sub (by exact measurable_const)\n165 |       (Measurable.const_mul h_meas_inner (1 / (N : ℝ)))) β\n166 |   exact h_term\n167 | \n168 | lemma productHaarMeasure_total_volume (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ) :\n169 |     productHaarMeasure N Λ sites (Set.univ : Set (FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites)) = 1 := by\n170 |   dsimp [productHaarMeasure]\n171 |   rw [MeasureTheory.Measure.pi_univ]\n172 |   let K : TopologicalSpace.PositiveCompacts (SU N) :=\n173 |     ⟨⟨Set.univ, isCompact_univ⟩, by simpa using Set.univ_nonempty (α := SU N)⟩\n174 |   have h_one : Measure.haarMeasure K (Set.univ : Set (SU N)) = 1 := by\n175 |     simpa [K] using Measure.haarMeasure_self (K₀ := K)\n176 |   have h_prod : (∏ _ : FiniteLinkIndex Λ sites, Measure.haarMeasure K (Set.univ : Set (SU N))) = 1 := by\n177 |     simp [h_one]\n178 |   simpa [K] using h_prod\n179 | \n180 | lemma productHaarMeasure_isFiniteMeasure (N : ℕ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] (sites : Finset Λ) :\n181 |     IsFiniteMeasure (productHaarMeasure N Λ sites) := by\n182 |   have h_total : productHaarMeasure N Λ sites (Set.univ : Set (FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites)) = 1 :=\n183 |     productHaarMeasure_total_volume N Λ sites\n184 |   refine { measure_univ_lt_top := ?_ }\n185 |   rw [h_total]\n186 |   exact ENNReal.one_lt_top\n187 | \n188 | /-- The partition function for a finite lattice with Wilson action. -/\n189 | noncomputable def partitionFunctionFinite (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] [AddVector Λ]\n190 |     (sites : Finset Λ) : ℝ :=\n191 |   ∫ (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites), Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)\n192 |     ∂ productHaarMeasure N Λ sites\n193 | \n194 | /-- The expectation value (Gibbs average) of an observable on a finite lattice. -/\n195 | noncomputable def gibbsExpectation (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] [AddVector Λ]\n196 |     (sites : Finset Λ) (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ) : ℝ :=\n197 |   let Z := partitionFunctionFinite N β Λ sites\n198 |   let μ₀ := productHaarMeasure N Λ sites\n199 |   (∫ (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites), f (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) *\n200 |     Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U) ∂ μ₀) / Z\n201 | \n202 | lemma partitionFunctionFinite_pos (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] [AddVector Λ]\n203 |     (sites : Finset Λ) : partitionFunctionFinite N β Λ sites > 0 := by\n204 |   haveI : IsProbabilityMeasure (productHaarMeasure N Λ sites) :=\n205 |     ⟨productHaarMeasure_total_volume N Λ sites⟩\n206 |   haveI : NeZero (productHaarMeasure N Λ sites) := by\n207 |     refine ⟨by\n208 |       intro hzero\n209 |       have hzero_univ : productHaarMeasure N Λ sites Set.univ = 0 := by simpa [hzero] using rfl\n210 |       rw [productHaarMeasure_total_volume N Λ sites] at hzero_univ\n211 |       exact one_ne_zero hzero_univ⟩\n212 |   by_cases h : sites = ∅\n213 |   · subst h\n214 |     dsimp [partitionFunctionFinite, wilsonActionFiniteConfig]\n215 |     simp [wilsonActionFinite]\n216 |   · dsimp [partitionFunctionFinite]\n217 |     apply integral_exp_pos\n218 |     have hmeas_exp : Measurable (λ (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) =>\n219 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)) := by\n220 |       refine Real.measurable_exp.comp\n221 |         (Measurable.const_mul (measurable_wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites) (-β))\n222 |     have h_bound : ∀ U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites,\n223 |       0 ≤ Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U) ∧\n224 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U) ≤ 1 := by\n225 |       intro U\n226 |       have h_nonpos : -β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U ≤ 0 := by\n227 |         have h_factor_nonneg : ∀ (n : Λ) (μ ν : Fin 4),\n228 |             0 ≤ 1 - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν :\n229 |               Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re) := by\n230 |           intro n μ ν\n231 |           let tr := (trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν :\n232 |             Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re\n233 |           have h_bound_tr : |tr| ≤ N :=\n234 |             trace_re_bound N (plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν)\n235 |           have h_tr_upper : tr ≤ N := by linarith [abs_le.mp h_bound_tr]\n236 |           have h_tr_lower : -N ≤ tr := by linarith [abs_le.mp h_bound_tr]\n237 |           by_cases hN0 : (N : ℝ) = 0\n238 |           · simp [hN0, tr]\n239 |           · have hpos : 0 < (N : ℝ) := by\n240 |               have hNpos' : 0 < N := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero (by\n241 |                 intro hzero\n242 |                 apply hN0\n243 |                 exact_mod_cast hzero)\n244 |               exact_mod_cast hNpos'\n245 |             have h_div_upper : (1 / (N : ℝ)) * tr ≤ 1 := by\n246 |               have h_mul : ((1 / (N : ℝ)) * tr) * (N : ℝ) ≤ 1 * (N : ℝ) := by\n247 |                 calc\n248 |                   ((1 / (N : ℝ)) * tr) * (N : ℝ) = tr := by field_simp [hN0]\n249 |                   _ ≤ N := h_tr_upper\n250 |                   _ = 1 * (N : ℝ) := by norm_num\n251 |               exact (mul_le_mul_iff_of_pos_right hpos).mp h_mul\n252 |             have h_div_lower : -1 ≤ (1 / (N : ℝ)) * tr := by\n253 |               have h_mul : (-1 : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) ≤ ((1 / (N : ℝ)) * tr) * (N : ℝ) := by\n254 |                 calc\n255 |                   (-1 : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) = -N := by ring\n256 |                   _ ≤ tr := h_tr_lower\n257 |                   _ = ((1 / (N : ℝ)) * tr) * (N : ℝ) := by field_simp [hN0]\n258 |               exact (mul_le_mul_iff_of_pos_right hpos).mp h_mul\n259 |             linarith\n260 |         have h_sum_nonneg : 0 ≤ ∑ n ∈ sites, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n261 |           (1 - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν :\n262 |             Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re)) := by\n263 |           refine Finset.sum_nonneg (λ n hn => Finset.sum_nonneg (λ μ hμ => Finset.sum_nonneg (λ ν hν => ?_)))\n264 |           exact h_factor_nonneg n μ ν\n265 |         have h_wilson_eq : wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U = β *\n266 |           (∑ n ∈ sites, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n267 |             (1 - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν :\n268 |               Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re))) := by\n269 |           dsimp [wilsonActionFiniteConfig, wilsonActionFinite, plaquetteContribution]\n270 |           calc\n271 |             ∑ n ∈ sites, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n272 |               β * ((1 : ℝ) - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν :\n273 |                 Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re))\n274 |                 = β * (∑ n ∈ sites, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n275 |                     ((1 : ℝ) - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν :\n276 |                       Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re))) := by\n277 |               simp_rw [Finset.mul_sum]\n278 |             _ = β * (∑ n ∈ sites, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n279 |                 (1 - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν :\n280 |                   Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re))) := rfl\n281 |         rw [h_wilson_eq]\n282 |         have h_sq_nonpos : -(β^2) ≤ 0 := by nlinarith [sq_nonneg β]\n283 |         set S := (∑ n ∈ sites, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n284 |           (1 - (1 / (N : ℝ)) * ((trace ((plaquetteProduct N (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) n μ ν :\n285 |             Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re))) with hS\n286 |         have h_mul_eq : -β * (β * S) = -(β^2) * S := by ring\n287 |         rw [h_mul_eq]\n288 |         exact mul_nonpos_of_nonpos_of_nonneg h_sq_nonpos h_sum_nonneg\n289 |       have h_exp_le_one : Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U) ≤ 1 :=\n290 |         (Real.exp_le_one_iff.mpr h_nonpos)\n291 |       have h_exp_nonneg : 0 ≤ Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U) :=\n292 |         (Real.exp_pos _).le\n293 |       exact ⟨h_exp_nonneg, h_exp_le_one⟩\n294 |     have h_int : Integrable (λ U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites =>\n295 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)) (productHaarMeasure N Λ sites) := by\n296 |       refine integrable_of_le_of_le hmeas_exp.aestronglyMeasurable\n297 |         (Filter.Eventually.of_forall (λ U => (h_bound U).1))\n298 |         (Filter.Eventually.of_forall (λ U => (h_bound U).2))\n299 |         (integrable_const (0 : ℝ))\n300 |         (integrable_const (1 : ℝ))\n301 |     exact h_int\n302 | \n303 | lemma gibbsExpectation_pos (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] [AddVector Λ]\n304 |     (sites : Finset Λ) (F : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ) (hF : ∀ U, F U ≥ 0) :\n305 |     gibbsExpectation N β Λ sites F ≥ 0 := by\n306 |   dsimp [gibbsExpectation]\n307 |   refine div_nonneg ?_ (le_of_lt (partitionFunctionFinite_pos N β Λ sites))\n308 |   apply integral_nonneg\n309 |   intro U\n310 |   exact mul_nonneg (hF (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U)) (le_of_lt (Real.exp_pos _))\n311 | \n312 | lemma gibbsExpectation_normalization (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] [AddVector Λ]\n313 |     (sites : Finset Λ) : gibbsExpectation N β Λ sites (λ _ => 1) = 1 := by\n314 |   dsimp [gibbsExpectation, partitionFunctionFinite]\n315 |   simp only [one_mul]\n316 |   exact div_self (ne_of_gt (partitionFunctionFinite_pos N β Λ sites))\n317 | \n318 | lemma gibbsExpectation_linear (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (Λ : Type) [DecidableEq Λ] [AddVector Λ]\n319 |     (sites : Finset Λ) (a b : ℝ) (F G : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ → ℝ)\n320 |     (hF : Integrable (λ (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) => F (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) *\n321 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)) (productHaarMeasure N Λ sites))\n322 |     (hG : Integrable (λ (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites) => G (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) *\n323 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)) (productHaarMeasure N Λ sites)) :\n324 |     gibbsExpectation N β Λ sites (λ U => a * F U + b * G U) =\n325 |     a * gibbsExpectation N β Λ sites F + b * gibbsExpectation N β Λ sites G := by\n326 |   dsimp [gibbsExpectation]\n327 |   set Z := partitionFunctionFinite N β Λ sites with hZ\n328 |   set μ₀ := productHaarMeasure N Λ sites with hμ₀\n329 |   have hZ_pos : Z ≠ 0 := by linarith [partitionFunctionFinite_pos N β Λ sites]\n330 |   -- Expand the numerator\n331 |   have h_num : (∫ (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites), ((a * F (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) + b * G (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U)) *\n332 |     Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)) ∂ μ₀) =\n333 |     a * (∫ (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites), (F (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) * Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)) ∂ μ₀) +\n334 |     b * (∫ (U : FiniteLinkConfig N Λ sites), (G (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) * Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)) ∂ μ₀) := by\n335 |     calc\n336 |       (∫ U, ((a * F (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) + b * G (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U)) *\n337 |         Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U)) ∂ μ₀)\n338 |           = (∫ U, (a * F (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) * Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β Λ sites U) +\n339 |               b * G (extendLinkVariable N Λ sites U) * Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFinite