{"id":19,"role":"Tool","content":"Search results (5):\n\n1. [https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-113/issue-3/General-proof-of-Osterwalder-Schrader-positivity-for-the-Wilson-action/cmp/1104160284.pdf]\n   PDF General Proof of Osterwalder-Schrader Positivity for the Wilson Action\n   Luscher [3] and independently Osterwalder and Seiler [4] have addressed the problem in two different ways. Luscher starting from the Wilson action builds up a Hubert space as a Fock space derived from equal time fields and explicitly constructs a transfer matrix [5] which he proves to be positive definite, in this context Osterwalder-Schrader positivity is proved for gauge invariant operators ...\n\n2. [https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01221251]\n   General proof of Osterwalder-Schrader positivity for the Wilson action ...\n   Abstract We extend the proof by Osterwalder and Seiler of reflection positivity of lattice gauge theories with fermions to the case in which the reflection is performed with respect to planes containing sites. Our proof applies to all observables and relies on the particular structure of the Wilson action.\n\n3. [https://inspirehep.net/literature/251466]\n   Osterwalder-schrader Positivity for the Wilson Action\n   Osterwalder-Seiler's proof of reflection positivity of lattice gauge theories with fermions is extended to the case in which the reflection is performed with respect to planes containing sites. Our proof applies to all observables and relies on the particular structure of the Wiklson action.\n\n4. [https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Osterwalder-schrader-positivity-for-the-wilson-Menotti-Pelissetto/a855dd3635438ec443264f8630f92cf1e5c43207]\n   Osterwalder-schrader positivity for the wilson action\n   Abstract Osterwalder-Seiler's proof of reflection positivity of lattice gauge theories with fermions is extended to the case in which the reflection is performed with respect to planes containing sites. Our proof applies to all observables and relies on the particular structure of the Wiklson action. This assures the positivity of the correlation function 〈ϑ(F)F〉 for any gauge invariant ...\n\n5. [https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Gauge-field-theories-on-a-lattice-Osterwalder-Seiler/610728f713f24d54488c5e5be85d5d96092211e3]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - Semantic Scholar\n   This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence and analyticity of the infinite volume limit of strongly coupled Yang-Mills theories on the lattice and we verify Wilson's confinement bound. Finally we present a rigorous treatment of the Higgs mechanism in lattice gauge theories.\n\n","timestamp":1783960295,"token_count":670,"tool_call_id":"call_00_LPVN2ZKR8Wt7uBylUDu40373","full_token_estimate":619,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"web_search","file_path":null,"old_text":"Osterwalder Seiler reflection positivity lattice gauge theory Wilson action Peter-Weyl transfer matrix","new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":null,"byte_count":2673,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":1278,"edit_line":null},"turn":7,"is_prune_marker":false}
